    "title": "New WrestleMania 42 Stipulation Raises Stakes for Pat McAfee’s Future",
    "text": "Pat McAfee has been revealed as the catalyst behind Randy Orton’s return to ruthless form—and honestly, it works.The road to WrestleMania 42 has already delivered its share of standout moments: Roman Reigns choosing CM Punk, Oba Femi getting the upper hand on Brock Lesnar, and Orton’s shocking turn on Cody Rhodes. Those moments helped shape the core of the card. McAfee’s alliance with Orton adds sauce on top.In true 2026 fashion, McAfee has taken over social media since his SmackDown appearance—none bigger than a late-night post that just raised the stakes of WrestleMania Saturday’s main event.ST LOUIS, MISSOURI - APRIL 3: Pat McAfee joins forces with Randy Orton during SmackDown at Enterprise Center on April 3, 2026 in St Louis, Missouri. (Photo by Georgiana Dallas/WWE via Getty Images)Getty Images (Getty Images)McAfee Puts His WWE Future on the LineMcAfee declared on X that if Orton fails to defeat Rhodes at WrestleMania, he will walk away from wrestling television for good.It’s a massive wrinkle in the Rhodes–Orton match. Sure, WWE could always pivot later if needed—but if McAfee is sticking around beyond WrestleMania, this stipulation feels telling. At the very least, it tilts the narrative—and the odds—toward Orton reclaiming the Undisputed WWE Championship.Why Is Pat McAfee Talking About Saving the Business?WWE Hall of Famer Mark Henry expanded on McAfee’s claims on Busted Open, earning a retweet from McAfee himself.Henry echoed the same philosophy: a return to bigger, stronger, more traditional stars like Orton, emphasizing a more old-school, smash-mouth, aggressive style reminiscent of what many fans associate with the Attitude Era.Did TKO Bring Pat McAfee Back?While McAfee continues to divide the WWE audience, the idea that his return was purely a top-down call from TKO executives feels oversimplified. However the deal came together, it was clearly collaborative—with Triple H fully invested.How to Watch WrestleMania 42ST LOUIS, MISSOURI - APRIL 3: Pat McAfee (R) punts Cody Rhodes (L) during SmackDown at Enterprise Center on April 3, 2026 in St Louis, Missouri. (Photo by Craig Melvin/WWE via Getty Images)Getty Images (Getty Images)Both nights of WrestleMania will take place in Las Vegas.Dates: Saturday, April 18 & Sunday, April 19, 2026Start Time: 6:00 p.m. ET / 5:00 p.m. CT / 3:00 p.m. PTLocation: Allegiant StadiumStreaming:United States: ESPNInternational: NetflixRelated: Related StoriesRelated: Oba Femi: Everything to Know About Brock Lesnar’s WrestleMania 42 OpponentThis story was originally published by Athlon Sports on Apr 4, 2026, where it first appeared in the Wrestling section. Add Athlon Sports as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
